WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.664 --> 00:02.599 align:center line:81%
In the parable of the prodigal son,

00:03.534 --> 00:06.637 align:center line:79%
the elder brother
initially struggled to celebrate

00:06.637 --> 00:11.475 align:center line:79%
when his younger brother returned home
after a period of poor choices

00:11.775 --> 00:14.444 align:center line:79%
and “wast[ing] his substance
with riotous living.”

00:15.646 --> 00:16.980 align:center line:81%
The elder brother's pride

00:16.980 --> 00:21.018 align:center line:79%
and self-righteousness kept
him from embracing the joy

00:21.018 --> 00:23.153 align:center line:81%
of his brother's repentant return.

00:24.288 --> 00:30.727 align:center line:79%
We also may let opportunities pass us
by without letting our loved ones know,

00:30.928 --> 00:34.932 align:center line:79%
through our words and actions,
of our sincere love for them.

00:35.866 --> 00:40.437 align:center line:79%
There are many powerful examples
in the scriptures of sincere love

00:40.470 --> 00:43.774 align:center line:81%
shared and received: Naomi and Ruth,

00:44.308 --> 00:45.876 align:center line:81%
Ammon and King Lamoni,

00:46.443 --> 00:51.315 align:center line:79%
the prodigal son and his father,
the Savior and His disciples.

00:52.316 --> 00:56.019 align:center line:79%
When love is freely
given and sincerely received,

00:56.320 --> 00:59.823 align:center line:81%
a virtuous cycle ensues with an increase

00:59.823 --> 01:03.026 align:center line:79%
of love between both
the giver and the receiver.

01:04.094 --> 01:09.366 align:center line:79%
God’s love is perfect,
infinite, enduring, and “most sweet.”

01:10.067 --> 01:13.303 align:center line:79%
It fills the soul
with “exceedingly great joy.”

01:14.137 --> 01:19.843 align:center line:79%
Nevertheless, at times we may find
it difficult to recognize God's love

01:20.110 --> 01:21.111 align:center line:81%
in our lives.

01:22.145 --> 01:25.382 align:center line:79%
However, our perfectly loving
Heavenly Father

01:25.782 --> 01:28.085 align:center line:81%
so deeply desires for us

01:28.085 --> 01:34.324 align:center line:79%
to experience His love that He “speaketh
unto [us] according to ... [our]

01:35.258 --> 01:41.531 align:center line:79%
understanding.” He will express His love
for us in ways we individually can

01:42.799 --> 01:47.638 align:center line:79%
recognize. We may experience God’s love
for us when we observe the beauties of

01:48.538 --> 01:50.674 align:center line:81%
nature, or receive answers to prayers,

01:51.541 --> 01:54.945 align:center line:79%
or have thoughts come
to our mind in the very moment of need,

01:55.846 --> 01:58.315 align:center line:81%
or experience sweet moments of joy.

01:59.816 --> 02:05.255 align:center line:79%
The greatest manifestation of Heavenly
Father's love for us that resonates

02:05.255 --> 02:07.257 align:center line:81%
with both mind and heart,

02:07.658 --> 02:12.496 align:center line:79%
is when He allowed His Beloved Son
to offer Himself as the atoning one.

02:13.797 --> 02:16.299 align:center line:81%
Like the prodigal son's elder brother,

02:16.933 --> 02:20.170 align:center line:81%
our focus is often centered on ourselves.

02:21.171 --> 02:25.242 align:center line:79%
We are so consumed with seeking evidence
of God's love for us,

02:25.976 --> 02:28.879 align:center line:79%
and we become frustrated
when we do not see it.

02:29.913 --> 02:34.985 align:center line:79%
But the beautiful paradox is that the more
we are focused on showing our love

02:34.985 --> 02:39.856 align:center line:79%
for God, the more easily
we recognize His love for us.

02:41.158 --> 02:44.661 align:center line:79%
Perhaps this is why the Savior
responded to the question,

02:44.961 --> 02:46.697 align:center line:81%
“Which is the great commandment?”

02:47.297 --> 02:50.233 align:center line:81%
with this simple and important invitation:

02:51.001 --> 02:56.106 align:center line:79%
“Thou shalt love the Lord thy God
with all thy heart, with all thy soul,

02:56.106 --> 02:57.574 align:center line:81%
and with all thy mind.”

02:58.842 --> 03:01.044 align:center line:81%
Sometimes the way we show our love

03:01.044 --> 03:06.516 align:center line:79%
to those we hold most dear is not
necessarily the way they recognize love.

03:07.551 --> 03:11.154 align:center line:79%
This may be frustrating for both
the giver and the receiver.

03:12.322 --> 03:16.827 align:center line:79%
It may be helpful to ask those we love
how they recognize love expressed.

03:17.894 --> 03:21.765 align:center line:79%
Likewise, if we want
to show our love for God,

03:22.032 --> 03:25.469 align:center line:79%
we should understand how
He recognizes our love.

03:26.536 --> 03:29.539 align:center line:79%
Fortunately, He has clearly
outlined several ways

03:29.539 --> 03:33.143 align:center line:79%
in the scriptures
that we can show our love for Him.

03:34.511 --> 03:37.314 align:center line:81%
In the instructive exchange between Peter

03:37.314 --> 03:40.117 align:center line:79%
and the resurrected Lord
at the Sea of Tiberius,

03:40.183 --> 03:42.986 align:center line:79%
we learn of ways we can show
our love for the Lord.

03:43.887 --> 03:48.859 align:center line:79%
“Jesus saith to Simon Peter,
Simon, son of Jonas,

03:49.226 --> 03:51.561 align:center line:81%
lovest thou me more than these?

03:52.395 --> 03:55.665 align:center line:79%
He saith unto him, Yea, Lord;
thou knowest that I love thee.”

03:57.000 --> 04:00.837 align:center line:79%
The key question
in this inquiry by the Lord is,

04:00.837 --> 04:03.006 align:center line:81%
“Lovest thou me more than these?”

04:04.074 --> 04:08.945 align:center line:79%
We show our love to the Lord
when we put Him above “these,”

04:09.613 --> 04:11.982 align:center line:81%
and “these” can be any one,

04:12.616 --> 04:18.021 align:center line:79%
any activity, or anything that displaces
Him from being the most

04:18.021 --> 04:20.290 align:center line:81%
important influence in our lives.

04:21.424 --> 04:25.061 align:center line:79%
There will never be enough time
in a day, a week,

04:25.362 --> 04:31.034 align:center line:79%
a month, or a year to get done
all we want or need to accomplish.

04:32.002 --> 04:36.673 align:center line:79%
Part of the test of mortality is to use
the precious resource of time

04:37.340 --> 04:40.243 align:center line:79%
for what is most important
for our eternal good,

04:40.644 --> 04:43.914 align:center line:79%
and to let go of those things
that are less important.

04:44.948 --> 04:50.620 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson said, “The
question for each of us ... is the same.

04:51.454 --> 04:56.193 align:center line:79%
... Are you willing to let God be the most
important influence in your life?

04:57.027 --> 05:00.397 align:center line:79%
Will you allow His words,
His commandments,

05:00.397 --> 05:04.067 align:center line:79%
and His covenants to influence
what you do each day?

05:05.202 --> 05:09.339 align:center line:79%
Will you allow His voice
to take priority over any other?

05:10.473 --> 05:12.876 align:center line:79%
Are you willing to let
whatever He needs you

05:12.876 --> 05:17.013 align:center line:79%
to do take precedence
over every other ambition?

05:18.081 --> 05:21.718 align:center line:79%
Are you willing to have your
will swallowed up in His?”

05:22.953 --> 05:26.756 align:center line:79%
We demonstrate our discipleship
and love for God

05:26.756 --> 05:29.326 align:center line:81%
when we make Him our top priority.

05:30.694 --> 05:34.965 align:center line:79%
In the next verse of this same
discussion between Peter and the Savior,

05:35.498 --> 05:36.933 align:center line:81%
we learn of another way

05:36.933 --> 05:39.769 align:center line:79%
the Lord recognizes
our expressions of love.

05:40.804 --> 05:46.176 align:center line:79%
“[The Lord] saith to him again the second
time, Simon, son of Jonas,

05:46.543 --> 05:51.982 align:center line:79%
lovest thou me? He saith unto him,
Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee.

05:52.983 --> 05:55.852 align:center line:81%
He saith unto him, Feed my sheep.”

05:56.920 --> 06:02.826 align:center line:79%
We show our love for Heavenly Father
when we serve, listen to, love,

06:03.059 --> 06:06.296 align:center line:81%
lift, or minister to His children.

06:07.297 --> 06:13.169 align:center line:79%
That service may be as simple
as truly seeing others without judgment.

06:14.037 --> 06:17.374 align:center line:79%
In the 76th section
of the Doctrine and Covenants,

06:17.574 --> 06:22.479 align:center line:79%
we get a glimpse of the character of those
who will inherit a celestial glory:

06:23.613 --> 06:27.784 align:center line:79%
“They see as they are seen,
and they know as they are known.”

06:28.618 --> 06:31.655 align:center line:81%
They see others as God sees them,

06:31.988 --> 06:37.227 align:center line:79%
and He sees them as they can become
with glorious divine potential.

06:38.595 --> 06:40.563 align:center line:81%
After returning home from my mission,

06:40.563 --> 06:45.068 align:center line:79%
I took over the lawn-care business my
brothers and I had started as teenagers.

06:45.669 --> 06:48.705 align:center line:79%
I was also busy
with my university studies.

06:49.673 --> 06:54.978 align:center line:79%
One spring week, heavy rains and looming
final exams left me overwhelmed

06:54.978 --> 06:56.713 align:center line:81%
and behind on yard work.

06:57.547 --> 07:02.419 align:center line:79%
Mid-week, the skies cleared, and I planned
to catch up on yard work after classes.

07:03.954 --> 07:07.891 align:center line:79%
But when I arrived home,
my truck and equipment were gone.

07:07.891 --> 07:10.527 align:center line:81%
Curious, I visited the scheduled yards.

07:10.694 --> 07:13.430 align:center line:79%
Each one had already been
beautifully trimmed.

07:14.097 --> 07:16.066 align:center line:81%
At the last yard on the schedule,

07:16.066 --> 07:18.868 align:center line:79%
I saw my younger brother
walking behind the mower.

07:19.636 --> 07:21.705 align:center line:81%
He saw me, smiled, and waved.

07:22.472 --> 07:25.608 align:center line:79%
Overcome with gratitude,
I hugged and thanked him.

07:26.309 --> 07:31.614 align:center line:79%
His meaningful act of service deeply
strengthened my love and loyalty for him.

07:32.415 --> 07:36.186 align:center line:79%
Serving each other is an unmistakable
way we show our love for God

07:36.186 --> 07:37.520 align:center line:81%
and His Beloved Son.

07:39.289 --> 07:43.493 align:center line:79%
We also manifest our love
for God by having a grateful heart.

07:44.427 --> 07:47.397 align:center line:79%
The Lord said, “In nothing
doth man offend God, ...

07:47.397 --> 07:50.667 align:center line:79%
save those who confess
not his hand in all things.”

07:51.468 --> 07:56.773 align:center line:79%
We show our love for God by acknowledging
Him as the source of every good thing

07:56.773 --> 07:57.774 align:center line:81%
in our lives.

07:58.842 --> 08:00.944 align:center line:81%
In the early days of launching a company,

08:01.011 --> 08:06.116 align:center line:79%
my business partner and I would pray
earnestly before important meetings asking

08:06.116 --> 08:07.717 align:center line:81%
for Heavenly Father's help.

08:08.518 --> 08:13.356 align:center line:79%
Time after time, God answered
our prayers and our meetings went well.

08:14.324 --> 08:18.428 align:center line:79%
After one meeting, my business
partner pointed out that we had been quick

08:18.428 --> 08:21.464 align:center line:81%
to ask for help but slow to give thanks.

08:22.198 --> 08:27.170 align:center line:79%
From then on, we made it a habit
to offer sincere prayers of gratitude,

08:27.670 --> 08:30.340 align:center line:79%
recognizing the Lord's hand
in our successes.

08:31.074 --> 08:34.544 align:center line:79%
We show our love for God
with an “attitude of gratitude.”

08:35.979 --> 08:38.314 align:center line:79%
Another way we show
our love for Heavenly Father

08:38.314 --> 08:42.218 align:center line:79%
and His Beloved
Son is to choose to obey Them.

08:43.386 --> 08:46.990 align:center line:79%
The Savior said, “If ye love me,
keep my commandments.”

08:47.857 --> 08:52.228 align:center line:79%
This kind of obedience is neither
blind nor compulsory,

08:52.729 --> 08:55.932 align:center line:79%
but is a sincere and willing
expression of love.

08:57.100 --> 09:00.804 align:center line:79%
Father in Heaven wants us
to want to be obedient.

09:02.105 --> 09:06.142 align:center line:79%
Sister Tamara W. Runia
called this “affectionate obedience.”

09:06.743 --> 09:11.114 align:center line:79%
She said, “Even though we don’t
have perfect obedience yet,

09:11.448 --> 09:13.583 align:center line:81%
we try affectionate obedience

09:13.616 --> 09:16.152 align:center line:81%
now, choosing to stay,

09:16.219 --> 09:18.822 align:center line:81%
again and again, because we love Him.”

09:20.190 --> 09:25.795 align:center line:79%
Heavenly Father gave us agency
to inspire us to want to choose Him.

09:26.629 --> 09:30.867 align:center line:79%
His work and glory is not only
to bring to pass our eternal life,

09:31.134 --> 09:37.240 align:center line:79%
but also includes a hope that our greatest
desire is to return to Him.

09:37.974 --> 09:40.477 align:center line:81%
However, He will never force us to obey.

09:41.678 --> 09:44.347 align:center line:79%
In the hymn “Know This,
That Every Soul Is Free,”

09:44.614 --> 09:51.554 align:center line:79%
we sing, “He’ll call, persuade,
direct aright, and bless with wisdom,

09:51.554 --> 09:54.424 align:center line:81%
love, and light. In nameless ways

09:54.491 --> 10:00.296 align:center line:79%
be good and kind, but never force
the human mind.” As mission leaders,

10:00.296 --> 10:03.833 align:center line:79%
my wife, Christina, and I were
inspired by so many missionaries

10:03.833 --> 10:09.172 align:center line:79%
who chose to be obedient not only
because it was a missionary standard,

10:09.572 --> 10:11.841 align:center line:81%
but because they wanted to show their love

10:11.841 --> 10:15.812 align:center line:79%
for the Lord by humbly choosing
to represent Him.

10:17.147 --> 10:19.082 align:center line:81%
Elder Dale G. Renlund said,

10:19.616 --> 10:22.352 align:center line:79%
“Our Heavenly Father’s
goal in parenting is not

10:22.352 --> 10:24.687 align:center line:81%
to have His children do what is right.

10:25.421 --> 10:28.791 align:center line:79%
It is to have His children
choose to do what is right

10:29.259 --> 10:31.394 align:center line:81%
and ultimately become like Him.

10:31.928 --> 10:34.264 align:center line:81%
If He simply wanted us to be obedient,

10:34.464 --> 10:39.169 align:center line:79%
He would use immediate rewards and
punishment to influence our behaviors.”

10:39.869 --> 10:44.174 align:center line:79%
We show our love for God when
we choose to obey and follow Him.

10:45.208 --> 10:50.547 align:center line:79%
Our Heavenly Father and our Savior
recognize our expressions of love for Them

10:50.914 --> 10:53.316 align:center line:81%
when we put Them first in our lives,

10:53.750 --> 10:58.488 align:center line:79%
serve one another, gratefully
acknowledge every blessing from Them,

10:58.955 --> 11:01.391 align:center line:81%
and choose to obey and follow Them.

11:02.091 --> 11:06.663 align:center line:79%
I testify that each one
of us truly is a child of God,

11:07.096 --> 11:08.898 align:center line:81%
and He loves us perfectly.

11:09.666 --> 11:15.371 align:center line:79%
I testify that He yearns for us to
experience His love in ways we recognize

11:15.371 --> 11:20.777 align:center line:79%
and understand. And the beautiful paradox
is that we will experience His love

11:20.777 --> 11:24.914 align:center line:79%
for us even more deeply
as we show our love for Him.

11:25.248 --> 11:27.550 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, Amen.

